{
  "schema": "research-public-artifact/v1",
  "concept": "Dementia with Lewy bodies and Parkinson's disease dementia",
  "slug": "dementia-with-lewy-bodies-and-parkinson-s-disease-dementia",
  "canonical_concept_id": "concept:2c5b86af5522c8ac2f148412d8f48dfacb960ccbd41d82617f0fa89857b1db3b",
  "canonical_artifact_sha256": "98c52b7a15262a52fb4b108de4af624f1f7e1fe2ddc9736ac8a99c326cdc8d5c",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "clm:2c4c7c54f4e3240870c2e68ab82e2e828ce2e898fa1c0525c9bc0928f7685e8b",
      "text": "A Neurology study comparing the alpha-synuclein seed amplification assay on CSF across 4 European laboratories, with 20 patients with DLB and 10 controls, reports average sensitivity of 78.8% (minimum 55%, maximum 100%) and average specificity of 77.5% (minimum 60%, maximum 100%). (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-01-28)",
      "source_url": "https://www.neurology.org/doi/10.1212/WNL.0000000000214614",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:038277314d6e3ddf3a5f73081937d9624f2d986d06247dec7539c490b804774b",
        "ev:7cc8f50c4da9286cc45b5b445e700ac048532e5822b1476d4daec76b21e24538",
        "ev:7f810492e91c65670cf2f1f7d28cfe4ace3f432aee61f02b8a2496647b1bb1d6",
        "ev:ada67e8f9761f2cd731b5ef7340fde8de45d108c55dad8f293afa4550b0ec379",
        "ev:e01a232006d90b7c841dfde26c29fe152316cb78032abc363a13a1cc81d781ca"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:c62be495c10900f1eda5864cba221c3d06f8d3ccaca0d8a79f7d70e8a476c49a",
      "text": "NINDS describes Lewy body dementia as including dementia with Lewy bodies and Parkinson\u2019s disease dementia. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.ninds.nih.gov/health-information/disorders/lewy-body-dementia",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:8f0c3262441568299136c7c1322ffeaca7ef00d2da829855aa669e53ad5c3595"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:d267269a0c8943e30bba9c0f94de3499ffc012999fcde6490da4b2598da5570f",
      "text": "The diagnostic-criteria review uses DLB for dementia before or concurrently with parkinsonism and PDD for dementia in well-established Parkinson\u2019s disease. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6987529/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:87228f74b9c1d357d4d073782b472086a840de96c30da535af1d168e6c442951"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:bd310a8c898bf0732b2ad233c39cda67e9b3f5ce2d7a0e01bdc8743e34156068",
      "text": "The diagnostic-criteria review lists fluctuating cognition, recurrent visual hallucinations, REM sleep behavior disorder and spontaneous parkinsonism as core clinical features of DLB. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6987529/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:411d407e60cae6790f1c3f22b9383f6fe1219e3fc24a5bd5c06cd78f64be0ff5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:fee024af70d9209fc4eb7c6824aad24d24106d376bc58498ec6368ef43b2c77c",
      "text": "The Movement Disorder Society task-force abstract characterizes Parkinson\u2019s disease dementia by impairment in attention, memory, executive and visuospatial functions. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17542011/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:dfd0f2740c7f0571b18e6b5d1c226dbd8bd972f8f579b4195be799e270041925"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:943ff85c0c113351a01a8155e257117aeab5235d5ba6719793be166730d77b8a",
      "text": "The Movement Disorder Society task-force abstract identifies Lewy body-type degeneration in cerebral cortex and limbic structures as the main pathological correlate of Parkinson\u2019s disease dementia. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17542011/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:e380d771025e1df62b0bb89ccf2e05542071e27321d5ff98fcf869ae64e7f959"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:f17b0e71d41f941278f36353c3fcc00d3733d975d65549bc3fbe159edc08cc99",
      "text": "The DLB Consortium identifies an increased risk of serious sensitivity reactions to antipsychotics in DLB. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5496518/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:50449cea8e517445e57fb99dd6d41d86b2af4932a5e8340b3fde1ef0395cb383"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:1aa43f28000acf46896d1ca40055b1198eaa9db3876d98fa20a4eec40b96839f",
      "text": "NINDS states that not all people with Parkinson\u2019s disease develop dementia and that predicting who will remains difficult. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.ninds.nih.gov/health-information/disorders/lewy-body-dementia",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:8a24aa0cf1dba9f11d13b2dfee33cb993d119c74c47ecc261b31a89f74ac6fa3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:22a275c0855e6cf17ae5b63687db522187b5ff232ecb0e09d5c0ac62ba569d08",
      "text": "The DLB Consortium notes that abundant neocortical neuritic plaques and tangles accompanying Lewy bodies can produce a clinical profile resembling Alzheimer disease rather than typical DLB. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5496518/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:1076553347876bea4ae76bad7328bb533f41962853e1c4db1fb051a533ec6eb0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:fd8fb206d7599cb3947d259dba4a3f24382f2590056c31fb743688698189af39",
      "text": "The consensus report considers the arbitrary timing cutoff clinically useful; the diagnostic-criteria review calls the 1-year rule operational with no scientific basis. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5496518/",
      "also": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6987529/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:1727da0e83adef1ea94e580238148787f36816b265eabdc3516fd3fce385d460",
        "ev:67d0f786701b03c7a44bbc427f5f620b9a98c8bc9bd95740d00e8bb567301e0e"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:43c78cba181fb3dd3997ee2dec0732db62b39887f6ffa1bd30c31e77187ae418",
      "text": "The DLB Consortium defines dementia interfering with normal social, occupational or daily functioning as essential for DLB diagnosis. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5496518/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:a141fe38d4ba335452b52461cbb729524eea2c4bd40de8713cd47db10c368d19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:7b209d9a4de472066b4b70d69fe5cd867f95e40eaddebce23c2b8e8ab2709cd9",
      "text": "The DLB Consortium describes disproportionate attentional, executive and visual-processing deficits relative to memory and naming as typical of DLB. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5496518/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:870848b5ced56a9ced056b3d424e1070f899aad2468cdbc4a533be55c5e0f35c"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:880991ab7ebf033ae73d7ba222977629c52cf7c0654965360866a5cf7ad5563c",
      "text": "The DLB Consortium states that normal dopamine-transporter uptake can occur in autopsy-confirmed DLB. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5496518/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:d617a7a9be4c7ab2acc60ecf262ff08a9f7a55cfc56d546ada23e9db388f0b79"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:1ef630552e7ebb320db67488c4fceeeda811274e8a2dff74578b814f927dd9c4",
      "text": "The DLB Consortium states that biomarkers alone do not establish probable DLB. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5496518/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:d826f6c98367dfff3056edc2fe899e09185df93671c03ffb60d749b42bb79218"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:338ea3ad81f84be32f612d78cc486880266986baa1da1fcc177e83c0864e2783",
      "text": "The DLB Consortium reports that trial meta-analyses support cholinesterase inhibitors for improving cognition, global function and activities of living in DLB. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5496518/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:c955bbdac83e667ddbcb5e775563498354f0a9fdb55d130dab43242a2fb43b95"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:7b3201dd7aa726e6ed29fe20f87655290e22a2ec14a0fe115c83668824c93705",
      "text": "The same Neurology study reports that SAA diagnostic performance varied across laboratories, with fair agreement of results (average \u03ba = 0.246), and its authors state that the findings highlight challenges for reproducibility across protocols. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-01-28)",
      "source_url": "https://www.neurology.org/doi/10.1212/WNL.0000000000214614",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:1ca6c54e3518b38a4331125bcd073324cce6ac62406f36f04287f7a17281adba",
        "ev:37cd0aa92fcea360b178eae18d72589e67b45b8960c212527ae4c09ffe7d8a23",
        "ev:7f810492e91c65670cf2f1f7d28cfe4ace3f432aee61f02b8a2496647b1bb1d6",
        "ev:9f90338e51a76e92b400850dcc043ae5ea59d97ec79bc2b43de1b4bbe3c1b804"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "narrative": [
    {
      "assertionId": "prose:d20472e7ca70d0f06ded44850e0e3996948a5e636fc45fe0e51cb95d605166ed",
      "statementSha256": "d20472e7ca70d0f06ded44850e0e3996948a5e636fc45fe0e51cb95d605166ed",
